     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a possible error.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg PO TID is 5,100 mg/day.** The FDA labeling maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, and that's the ceiling even with normal kidney and liver function. At 5,100 mg/day, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is substantial. Also, 1700 mg isn't a standard tablet strength (500, 850, and 1000 mg are the usual IR options).\n\nSome possibilities:\n- **Intended 850 mg TID** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum, with meals)\n- **Intended 1000 mg BID** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **Intended 500 mg TID** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **Intended 1700 mg total per day**, which would be a different schedule entirely\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm 1700 mg TID if that's deliberate and you want it entered as written. I'll enter the order once you confirm."
      }
     ],
